!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-reference-to-a-constructor-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.1, [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    A reference, `ref<T>`, names a value of the type `T`, so `T` is a type of the writer's own namespace and
    never a constructor: the names of the types built with a constructor are a kind, and `kind<record>` is
    that spelling. `ref<record>` is refused where it is written.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
